# font-util -- the font root directory, declared once so that two other
# packages stop each guessing it.
#
# It ships almost nothing: two small tools, seventeen encoding map files, an
# aclocal macro, and fontutil.pc. The .pc is the point. It carries one variable,
#
#     fontrootdir=/usr/share/fonts/X11
#
# and both libfontenc and Xwayland resolve their own paths from it:
#
#   libfontenc  configure line 19894 -- `FONTROOTDIR=$($PKG_CONFIG --variable=
#               fontrootdir fontutil)`, falling back to ${datadir}/fonts/X11.
#   xwayland    meson.build 142-149 -- `dependency('fontutil', required:false)`,
#               falling back to the same literal.
#
# WHAT THIS PACKAGE IS AND IS NOT FOR, because the honest version is narrower
# than it first looks. Both fallbacks above name the same directory this package
# names, so on THIS tree the paths come out identical either way -- packaging it
# does not rescue a path that would otherwise be wrong. What it does is make the
# two consumers agree by construction rather than by coincidence, and give the
# directory an owner, so that moving it later is one edit rather than three.
#
# And Xwayland does NOT depend on any of these directories existing. dix/main.c
# 229-231 fatals when it cannot open the font "fixed", but libXfont2 compiles
# that font into itself and dix/dixfonts.c:1716 appends "built-ins" to every
# font path -- so the builtin is what actually keeps the server alive. See
# pkgs/libXfont2, which asserts it. Nothing in this tree installs a single file
# into fonts/X11/misc, TTF, OTF, Type1, 100dpi or 75dpi, and Xwayland logs a
# warning per missing element and carries on.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://www.x.org/pub/individual/font/font-util-1.4.1.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=5c9f64123c194b150fee89049991687386e6ff36ef2af7b80ba53efaf368cc95
SRC_DIR=font-util-1.4.1

# --with-fontrootdir IS STATED EVEN THOUGH IT MATCHES THE DEFAULT, because the
# default is `${datadir}/fonts/X11` (configure.ac:41) and ${datadir} is decided
# by --prefix. That is a substitution rather than a constant, and the whole
# value of this package is that the string it publishes is the one everybody
# else reads. Writing it out means a change to it is a change to this line
# rather than a consequence of one somewhere else.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--with-fontrootdir=/usr/share/fonts/X11"
